Now, you could manually use the Pythagorean Theorem, but you can just spot the <imath>45^\circ-45^\circ-90^\circ</imath> triangle and see <imath>\overline{ED}=5</imath>.  After this, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the length of <imath>\overline{CE}</imath>. <cmath>5^2+(5-x)^2   = (\overline{CE})^2 </cmath> 
<cmath> 25+25+x^2-10x = (\overline{CE})^2 </cmath> 
<cmath> x^2-10x+50 = (\overline{CE})^2 </cmath> <cmath> \sqrt{x^2-10x+50}=\overline{CE}</cmath>
From this, we can see that <imath>\overline{CB} = 7-\overline{CE} \implies \overline{CB} = 7 - \sqrt{x^2-10x+50}</imath>
